course: dictionary
lesson: 5053
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word inquiry can mean a question you ask to find something out, an official investigation into what really happened, or, in science, learning by asking and testing questions. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: Look for clues. In «Helping police with their inquiries», the word police is the clue. This inquiry is a police investigation, and the phrase means being questioned as a suspect, which is someone the police think may have done the crime.
explain: Ask yourself what the topic is. In a science lesson, inquiry means testing questions. In a news report about a disaster, it means an official investigation. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Inquiry means a question you ask to get information.
fact: An official inquiry is an investigation to find out the truth about something, such as an accident.
fact: In school science, inquiry means learning by asking questions and testing them.
fact: Inquiry can also be spelled enquiry, and both spellings are used in science lessons.
fact: «Helping police with their inquiries» is a British phrase meaning being questioned as a suspect.
exercise: Sam asks at the desk, «Can I make an inquiry about my lost bag?» What is an inquiry here? | A kind of bag | A test you do in a science lab | A police investigation into a crime | *A question you ask to get information
exercise: «The government held an inquiry into the flood.» What is an inquiry here? | A shop counter for buying tickets | *An official investigation to find out the truth | A game played at school | A question you ask a friend
exercise: In science, Mia learns by asking questions and testing them. What is this called? | Enquiry in the sense of a shopping list | Drawing a picture of a plant | Reading aloud | *Inquiry
test: «The police asked him to come in, as part of their inquiries.» What does helping police with their inquiries mean? | Helping to clean the police station | *Being questioned as a suspect | Winning a prize from the police | Going on holiday
test: Which sentence uses inquiry to mean an official investigation? | Lily likes to ask lots of questions about the stars | The class did a science project on plants | Ben made an inquiry about the time of the bus | *The government set up an inquiry into the train crash
exam: What is the best way to check which meaning of inquiry fits a sentence? | Pick the first meaning you remember, without reading the sentence | Count the letters in the word | Read the sentence backwards | *Swap your chosen meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
